This question involves methods that distribute text across lines of an electronic sign. The electronic sign
and the text to be displayed on it are represented by the  Sign  class. You will write the
complete  Sign  class, which contains a constructor and two methods.
The  Sign  class constructor has two parameters. The first parameter is a  String  that contains the
message to be displayed on the sign. The second parameter is an  int  that contains the width of each
line of the sign. The width is the positive maximum number of characters that can be displayed on a
single line of the sign.
A sign contains as many lines as are necessary to display the entire message. The message is split among
the lines of the sign without regard to spaces or punctuation. Only the last line of the sign may contain
fewer characters than the width indicated by the constructor parameter.
The following are examples of a message displayed on signs of different widths. Assume that in each
example, the sign is declared with the width specified in the first column of the table and with the
message  "Everything on sale, please come in",  which contains 34 characters.
